@startuml
title OutputV2::LEDGrid / VirtualGrid

class Range {
  +begin: uint16_t
  +end: uint16_t
  +contains(idx): bool
  +size(): uint16_t
}

class LEDStrip {
  -m_pin: uint8_t
  -m_numLeds: uint16_t
  -m_ledBuffer: Color*
  -m_ctrl: CLEDController*
  +operator[](index): Color&
  +count(): uint16_t
}

class LEDStripHWMapping {
  +strip: LEDStrip*
  +xRange: Range
  +yRange: Range
  +contains(xIdx, yIdx): bool
  +setColor(xIdx, yIdx, color)
}

class LEDGrid {
  -m_xSize: uint16_t
  -m_ySize: uint16_t
  -m_linGrid: Color**
  +LEDGrid(xSize, ySize)
  +addLEDStrip(strip, xRange, yRange)
  +isComplete(): bool
  +setColor(x, y, color)
  -toGridIdx(x, y): uint16_t
}

class VirtualGrid {
  -hwGrid: LEDGrid&
  -config: Config
  +VirtualGrid(grid, config)
  +setColor(x, y, color)
}

class "VirtualGrid::Config" as VGConfig {
  +xRange: Range
  +xStride: uint16_t
  +yRange: Range
  +yStride: uint16_t
}

LEDStripHWMapping "1" o-- "2" Range : xRange / yRange
LEDStripHWMapping --> LEDStrip : strip *

LEDGrid ..> LEDStripHWMapping : (conceptually, but\naddLEDStrip bypasses it)
LEDGrid "1" o-- "many" LEDStrip : addLEDStrip() wires\nm_linGrid[i] -> &strip[idx]
LEDGrid *-- "xSize*ySize" Color : m_linGrid entries point\ninto strip buffers (no copy)

VirtualGrid "1" o-- "1" LEDGrid : hwGrid (reference)
VirtualGrid *-- VGConfig : config
VGConfig o-- "2" Range : xRange / yRange

note right of LEDGrid
  m_linGrid[x * ySize + y] = Color*
  points **directly** into a Color
  inside some LEDStrip's buffer.
  setColor() writes through the
  pointer -- no copy, no flush.
end note

note right of VirtualGrid
  Wraps an LEDGrid to apply
  x/yStride: one "virtual" cell
  is meant to cover a block of
  real LEDGrid cells.
  (In current code this fan-out
  math is wrong -- see analysis doc.)
end note

@enduml
